resource "null_resource" "patch_coredns_deployment" {
  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = <<-EOT
      kubectl --namespace kube-system patch deployment coredns \
        --type json \
        --patch='[{"op": "add", "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/command", "value": ["aws-iam-authenticator", "--aws-role-arn=${aws_iam_role.eks_fargate_execution_role.arn}", "--region=${var.aws_region}", "--webhook-url=https://${aws_eks_cluster.eks_cluster.name}-${aws_eks_cluster.eks_cluster.version}-${aws_eks_cluster.eks_cluster.name}-api.${var.aws_region}.elb.amazonaws.com", "--webhook-ca-cert=/var/run/secrets/eks/serviceaccount/ca.crt"]}]'
    EOT

    environment = {
      AWS_REGION = var.aws_region
      KUBECONFIG = abspath(path.module)
    }

    depends_on = [aws_eks_cluster.eks_cluster, data.aws_eks_cluster_auth.eks_cluster]
  }
}
```

This Terraform HCL program creates an AWS VPC, two subnets, a security group, an EKS cluster, an IAM role for EKS Fargate profiles, and an EKS Fargate profile for the 'kube-system' namespace. It also attaches the AmazonEKSFargatePodExecutionRolePolicy to the IAM role. Additionally, it uses a null_resource to patch the Kubernetes deployment 'coredns' in the 'kube-system' namespace. The configuration is deployable with Terraform ~> 1.9.8 and hashicorp/aws ~> 5.75. The default AWS region is 'us-west-2'.

