This Terraform configuration creates a DynamoDB table, a CloudWatch log group and log stream, an IAM role, IAM policy, and IAM policy attachment to enable AWS Contributor Insights on the specified table. The table name is "ExampleTableName" as specified in the prompt. The log group and log stream are created with the appropriate names derived from the table name. The IAM role, policy, and policy attachment are created to allow the DynamoDB table to send logs to CloudWatch for contributor insights. The IAM role is assumed by the DynamoDB service. The IAM policy allows the necessary CloudWatch actions for contributor insights. The IAM policy attachment attaches the policy to the IAM role. Finally, the `aws_dynamodb_table_contributor_insights` resource is created to enable contributor insights on the specified table.

