This Terraform HCL program sets up a basic AWS Neptune cluster with a custom parameter group that only allows connection from two example subnets. The VPC, subnets, security group, Neptune cluster, custom parameter group, and association are all created as specified in the prompt. The CIDR blocks for the subnets are set to default values for demonstration purposes, but should be replaced with the desired subnet CIDRs. The security group allows inbound traffic only from the specified subnets on port 3306 (the default Neptune port). The Neptune cluster is created with a single availability zone and the custom parameter group is associated with it.

