This Terraform configuration creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an Elastic IP. It includes an ALB, a target group, a listener, an Elastic IP, and an attachment between the target group and the Elastic IP. The configuration also includes a VPC, security group, and subnets, which are necessary for creating an ALB. The security group allows all incoming traffic for simplicity, but you should replace it with a more secure configuration in a production environment.

